                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f6f8b' fontsize='16'>Key findings</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>• Default rises steadily from 5.</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>5% (AA) t</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>o 26</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>.5% (G). </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>The rating is the clearest risk driver.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>• F- and G-rated loans default almost 5× m</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>ore tha</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>n AA loans.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>• Weak ratings + medium/long loans are the riskiest: </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>G 13–36 months = 29.7%</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>, </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>F 37–60 months = 27.6%</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>Æ </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='7'>W</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
