          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#1f6f8b' fontsize='16'>Key findings</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>• Weak ratings + medium/long loans are the riskiest: G 13–36 months = 29.7%, F 37–60 months = 27.6%</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>• Latvia: even A-rated loans default about 30%, so the rating alone isn’t enough there</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#333333' fontsize='12'>• Short loans (up to 12 months) stay low-risk in almost every rating</run>
          </formatted-text>
